# versions.env — the single source of truth for every third-party version this
# project installs.
#
# Sourced by bootstrap-aws.sh, bootstrap-azure.sh and scripts/set-failure-policy.sh.
# The workflows apply their own pins; scripts/version-audit.sh checks all of them
# against what upstream currently publishes, and scripts/bump-versions.sh moves
# them forward in one place.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TWO SETS OF NUMBERS, AND THE DIFFERENCE MATTERS
#
#   INSTALL_*   what the next bootstrap will install.
#   RESULTS_*   what the artefacts committed under results/ were collected on.
#
# When they differ, results/ describes a cluster that no longer exists. That is
# a legitimate state to be in — it is where this repository sits right now,
# deliberately — but it must be visible, so the bootstraps print a banner and
# scripts/version-audit.sh reports it.
#
# Move RESULTS_* forward only after the affected experiments have actually been
# re-run and their artefacts committed. Never as part of the same edit that
# moves INSTALL_*.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── What the next bootstrap installs ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Updated 2026-08-02 to the current releases, by decision: the next destroy/apply
# rebuilds on the latest of everything.
#
# Chart version and application version are different numbers, and the
# dissertation must name the application one (defect D12).
KYVERNO_CHART_VERSION="3.8.2"
KYVERNO_APP_VERSION="v1.18.2"

# Cosign 3.x is a MAJOR version change from the 2.2.3 the evaluation used. The
# first pipeline run after this upgrade must confirm that Kyverno can still
# verify what Cosign produces — see the note in scripts/version-audit.sh.
#
# ── COSIGN IS HELD AT 2.x DELIBERATELY. THIS IS A RESULT, NOT AN OVERSIGHT ───
#
# Cosign 3.x was pinned here on 2026-08-02 and reverted on 2026-08-15 after it
# was measured to be incompatible with the admission controller. Defect D32.
#
# What was observed, on image
#   …/supply-chain/hello-world@sha256:e43a0d3e…  (run 31884945589):
#
#   * `cosign verify` with Cosign v3.1.2                     PASS
#   * `cosign tree` reports every artefact stored "via OCI referrer" —
#       sigstore.dev/cosign/sign/v1, cyclonedx.org/bom, slsa.dev/provenance/v1
#   * the legacy tags sha256-<digest>.sig and .att              404, absent
#   * Kyverno v1.18.2 reads the legacy tags and reports  "no signatures found"
#
# Cosign 3.0 made three changes on by default at once — the protobuf bundle
# format, OCI 1.1 referring artifacts, and TUF-provided service URLs — and
# REMOVED the `--new-bundle-format` flag that used to switch the first off.
# `cosign sign` still has `--registry-referrers-mode=legacy`, but **`cosign
# attest` does not**, so the two attestation policies could not be satisfied by
# any flag combination. There is no configuration of Cosign 3 that this
# admission controller can verify, and policies/verify-*.yaml is not editable.
#
# v2.6.5 is the newest 2.x (published 2026-08-06, maintained) and is what the
# workflows now install. sigstore/cosign-installer stays at v4.1.2 — it branches
# on the cosign major and handles the 2.x `.sig` asset layout on its legacy path.
#
# DO NOT "fix" this by bumping to 3.x. It is the finding. See changes.md §21.
COSIGN_VERSION="v2.6.5"
SYFT_VERSION="v1.50.0"

# Harness only — stages the E3 attestation-replay case. Nothing verifies it and
# no result depends on its version.
CRANE_VERSION="v0.21.8"

# Kubernetes is left where it is: the EKS nodes already run v1.34.x, which is
# current. Recorded so the audit can report it rather than leaving it implicit.
K8S_EXPECTED_MINOR="1.34"

# ── What the committed results describe ──────────────────────────────────────
# Every artefact under results/ was collected against this stack. Each artefact
# also records its own run.kyverno_image, so any single result can be checked
# against this line.
#
# DO NOT move these until the experiments have been re-run on the new stack.
# Moved forward 2026-08-15, after — and only after — the whole AWS programme was
# re-run on this stack and the artefacts committed: pipeline test cases
# (31885975456), attack suite fail-open (31886676002) and fail-closed
# (31887855859), evasion on main (31888272847) and on a branch (31888450460),
# latency cache-off (31892458755) and cache-on (31893322126), concurrency
# cache-off (31894663949) and cache-on (31895209590), size cache-on
# (31894106144) and cache-off (31896370075), SLSA L2 evidence (31885975456).
#
# `results/MANIFEST.md` lists every artefact with the stack it was collected on,
# derived from the artefacts rather than from this comment.
#
# ⚠️ AZURE IS NOT YET COLLECTED ON THIS STACK. These lines describe the AWS
# artefacts. Nothing under results/ describes an Azure cluster at any version —
# the earlier Azure data was invalidated and deleted (defect D18).
RESULTS_KYVERNO_CHART="3.8.2"
RESULTS_KYVERNO_APP="v1.18.2"
RESULTS_COSIGN="v2.6.5"
RESULTS_SYFT="v1.50.0"
